From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemdisp/tests: Measure direct WMI method invocation.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Offline Windows 10 executes direct StdRegProv methods with METHOD and
METHOD | PROPERTYGET, returning the provider's status and copying out
the values. Winum 11.22-2 rejected both flag combinations. Use a synthetic
per-run HKCU key to cover the measured arguments and output types.

diff --git a/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/Makefile.in b/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/Makefile.in
index 5614c4e..9289a8d 100644
--- a/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/Makefile.in
@@ -2 +2 @@ TESTDLL   = wbemdisp.dll
-IMPORTS   = oleaut32 ole32
+IMPORTS   = oleaut32 ole32 advapi32
@@ -4,0 +5 @@ SOURCES = \
+	method.c \
diff --git a/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/method.c b/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/method.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1ce53c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/wbemdisp/tests/method.c
@@ -0,0 +1,206 @@
+/*
+ * Direct WMI method invocation tests
+ *
